@anon.66d731aad004fadc267d2ec7cc952fb9.82 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [721 x i8] }> <{ [721 x i8] c"Output fixed-size pieces of INPUT to PREFIXaa, PREFIXab, ...; default size is 1000, and default PREFIX is 'x'. With no INPUT, or when INPUT is -, read standard input.\0A\0AThe SIZE argument is an integer and optional unit (example: 10K is 10*1024).\0AUnits are K,M,G,T,P,E,Z,Y,R,Q (powers of 1024) or KB,MB,... (powers of 1000).\0ABinary prefixes can be used, too: KiB=K, MiB=M, and so on.\0A\0ACHUNKS may be:\0A\0A- N       split into N files based on size of input\0A- K/N     output Kth of N to stdout\0A- l/N     split into N files without splitting lines/records\0A- l/K/N   output Kth of N to stdout without splitting lines/records\0A- r/N     like 'l' but use round robin distribution\0A- r/K/N   likewise but only output Kth of N to stdout" }>, align 1
